\subsection{Adaptive Inference-Time Compute}
\label{sec:adaptive_k_method}

Experiments reveal that unconditional correction is harmful: CRM applied at every step degrades all four LIBERO suites (up to $-$14.8\,pp; Section~\ref{sec:failure_modes}). The ${\sim}$80--97\% of steps where the VLA is already confident receive corrections that are noise. The solution is a per-step uncertainty probe that decides \emph{when} to apply correction.

